ame>Safford</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Pogach</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Who has diabetes? Best estimates of diabetes prevalence in the Department of Veterans Affairs based on computerized patient data</article-title><source>Diabetes Care</source><year>2004</year><volume>27</volume><issue>Suppl 2</issue><fpage>B10</fpage><lpage>B21</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2337/diacare.27.suppl_2.B10</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Miller DR, Safford MM, Pogach LM. Who has diabetes? Best estimates of diabetes prevalence in the Department of Veterans Affairs based on computerized patient data. Diabetes Care. May 2004;27 Suppl 2:B10&#x02013;21. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15113777</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR6"><label>6.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reiber</surname><given-names>GE</given-names></name><name><surname>Boyko</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Maynard</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Koepsell</surname><given-names>TD</given-names></name><name><surname>Pogach</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Diabetes in the Department of Veterans Affairs</article-title><source>Diabetes Care</source><year>2004</year><volume>27</volume><issue>Suppl 2</issue><fpage>B1</fpage><lpage>B2</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2337/diacare.27.suppl_2.B1</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Reiber GE, Boyko EJ, Maynard C, Koepsell TD, Pogach LM. Diabetes in the Department of Veterans Affairs. Diabetes Care. May 2004;27 Suppl 2:B1&#x02013;2. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15113775</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reiber</surname><given-names>GE</given-names></name><name><surname>Koepsell</surname><given-names>TD</given-names></name><name><surname>Maynard</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Haas</surname><given-names>LB</given-names></name><name><surname>Boyko</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Diabetes in nonveterans, veterans, and veterans receiving Department of Veterans Affairs health care</article-title><source>Diabetes Care</source><year>2004</year><volume>27</volume><issue>Suppl 2</issue><fpage>B3</fpage><lpage>B9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2337/diacare.27.suppl_2.B3</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Reiber GE, Koepsell TD, Maynard C, Haas LB, Boyko EJ. Diabetes in nonveterans, veterans, and veterans receiving Department of Veterans Affairs health care. Diabetes Care. May 2004;27 Suppl 2:B3&#x02013;9. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15113776</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Prochaska</surname><given-names>JO</given-names></name><name><surname>Velicer</surname><given-names>WF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The transtheoretical model of health behavior change</article-title><source>Am J Health Promot</source><year>1997</year><volume>12</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>38</fpage><lpage>48</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Prochaska JO, Velicer WF. The transtheoretical model of health behavior change. Am J Health Promot. Sep&#x02013;Oct 1997;12(1):38&#x02013;48. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10170434</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bandura</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Self-efficacy: Toward a unifying theory of behavioral change</article-title><source>Psychol Rev</source><year>1977</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>191</fpage><lpage>245</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1037/0033-295X.84.2.191</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Bandura A. Self-efficacy: Toward a unifying theory of behavioral change. Psychol Rev. 1977;8:191&#x02013;245. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">847061</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Freedman</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Deci</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Supporting autonomy to motivate patients with diabetes for glucose control</article-title><source>Diabetes Care</source><year>1998</year><volume>21</volume><issue>10</issue><fpage>1644</fpage><lpage>1651</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2337/diacare.21.10.1644</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Williams G, Freedman Z, Deci E. Supporting autonomy to motivate patients with diabetes for glucose control. Diabetes Care. October 1, 1998 1998;21(10):1644&#x02013;1651. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9773724</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Funnell</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Butler</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Arnold</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Fitzgerald</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name><name><surname>Feste</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Patient empowerment. Results of a randomized controlled trial</article-title><source>Diabetes Care</source><year>1995</year><volume>18</volume><issue>7</issue><fpage>943</fpage><lpage>949</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2337/diacare.18.7.943</pub-id></c